Gadi
====
This is a guide for running JigSeq PuzzleApp on Gadi.

Usage
-----
1. The simplest way is to SSH through a terminal.

SSH into Gadi and forward local TCP port 1337 to remote address 127.0.0.1:9461:

	ssh -L 1337:127.0.0.1:9461 <user>@gadi.nci.org.au

Load R version 4.3.1:

	module load R/4.3.1

Run the app given an R library and a pre-generated RData file:

	R_LIBS_USER=<Rlib> OUTDIR=<dir> ./run.R <RData> 9461

For example:

	R_LIBS_USER=/g/data/kr68/andre/R_libs/ OUTDIR=out ./run.R /g/data/kr68/andre/APP_TEST/App_Data/RBW401/pipeface-v0.1.0/20240821-210312/RBW401.RData 9461

Connect to <http://127.0.0.1:1337> using a browser on your local machine.

2. The next method only requires a web browser.

Open the following url and login to NCI:

	<https://are.nci.org.au/pun/sys/dashboard/batch_connect/sys/rstudio/ncigadi/session_contexts/new>

Provide the following options:

	Advanced Options -> Modules: R/4.3.1
	                 -> Environment Variables: R_LIBS_USER=<Rlib>,OUTDIR=<dir>

If you are using non-local directories for R_LIBS_USER and/or OUTDIR, you will
need to specify them in the "Storage" option. For example,

	Project: kr68
	Storage: gdata/kr68+scratch/kr68
	Advanced Options -> Modules: R/4.3.1
	                 -> Environment Variables: R_LIBS_USER=/g/data/kr68/andre/R_libs/R_LIBS_USER,OUTDIR=/scratch/kr68/user/out

Click "Launch". Wait for the session to start running. Then, click "Connect to
RStudio Server".

In the Console run the following R commands:

	load(<RData>)
	shiny::runApp(<path_to_puzzleapp>)

For example:

	load('/g/data/kr68/andre/APP_TEST/App_Data/RBW401/pipeface-v0.1.0/20240821-210312/RBW401.RData')
	shiny::runApp('/g/data/kr68/andre/puzzleapp')

The Shiny app should automatically open in a new tab or window.
